<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25077" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ,
			i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰσσός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of
			Cilicia</i>, <i>on the Mediterranean</i> (<i>the Gulf of Issus</i>, now <i>Gulf of
				Iskenderun</i>), <i>at the foot of Mount
			Amanus</i>, <i>where Darius was defeated by
			Alexander</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 13, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 27,
				22, § 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				2, 10, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 3, 8, 8</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Issĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Issus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				<i>the Gulf of Issus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					1, 13, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 108, 112, §
		243</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
